window.docContents[10].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Theorem-files/Symbolic.Theorems.RefinementPreservation/#file-Symbolic___Theorems___RefinementPreservation":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Theorems › RefinementPreservation.leanTier 1 · theorem file\n\nTier 1 · theorem file used by the symbolic proof 1 headline theorem 53 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. This file states headline theorems. Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nCited in the paper* Proof sketch, §5.1.5: comp_refinement_preservation_cli\n\n\n\nSecurity Preservation Across CLI Trace RefinementTrusted: the statement.Proves comp_refinement_preservation_cli (CompRefinementPreservationCli Agree R, Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/RefinementPreservation.lean): for any hook agreement predicate Agree and CLI run relation R, if the ten symbolic security properties hold in the composed model and R refines the model from initDirs, then all ten properties hold on guarded, coin-fresh hardware execution traces against HwAttackerKnows up to cryptographic collisions.Instantiating Agree and R with HooksMatchInterpretation and elfRelPlaced mpl mmpl elf (Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/ElfBinding.lean) combines Symbolic/Theorems/ModelSecurity.lean with comp_refines_cli_placed (Symbolic/Theorems/Refinement.lean) to yield signal_session_secure_placed (Symbolic/Theorems/Security.lean).\n\n\n\ntheorem comp_refinement_preservation_cliL43–54 ↗#Generic security preservation over CLI runs (CompRefinementPreservationCli Agree R, Symbolic/Specifications/Refinement/RefinementPreservation.lean): the ten composed model security theorems together with trace refinement (CompRefinesCli Agree R) imply binary-level security on all guarded, coin-fresh traces (SignalSessionSecureFor Agree R, Symbolic/Specifications/Security/Binary.lean).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Theorems/RefinementPreservation.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Theorem-files/Symbolic.Theorems.RefinementPreservation/#file-Symbolic___Theorems___RefinementPreservation"}});